# Swift conventions

- Imports at the top of the file. No inline imports.
- Switch over a union or enum: exhaustive, `never` in `default`.
- App and feature targets are `MainActor` by default. Library modules (`SystemKit`, `ControlSurface`, `PrivateAPI`) stay `nonisolated`. Background work needs an explicit `@concurrent` or a nonisolated type — do not assume `nonisolated async` hops off the caller.
- Features expose `convenience init(context:)` plus a designated init with injected system seams.
- Settings only through `context.settings`. Commands return `String`.
- Do not talk to the menu bar, hotkeys or CLI from a feature.
- Private API: pair every `dlsym` / bridged symbol with a resolve test like `SkyLightAvailabilityTests`.
- Prefer `buildableFolders`. `tuist generate` only after adding a module.
